  },
  {
    "episode_id": 88023,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88023.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, there were two moments. The first, there were three moments. The first moment was after he got elected. And in America, we all found out that Russia tried to help him get elected. And right away, instead of caring about that, all Donald Trump cared about was he didn't want anything to tarnish his victory. So he got in the way of the investigation into Russia from the beginning. The second point for me was after he became president, and I really started to pay attention to the guy. Oh my God. I found out that he lies every time he opens his mouth. That's not an exaggeration. He lies every time he opened his mouth. I couldn't support that. The final straw for me was Helsinki in the summer of 2018, when he had that summit with Putin. And in front of the world, Donald Trump said, I believe Putin and not my own American intelligence community. To me, that was the greatest act of disloyalty I've ever seen in an American president. I'm on the radio all over the country that night. I go on the radio that night. And as a conservative, I tell my audience, I'm going to do everything I can to make sure this son of a bitch doesn't get reelected. And from that moment on, I began to lose everything.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
