    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88023.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "It's like, it's like, look, I went to Congress 10 years ago and I had a reputation as kind of the angry tea party guy. The election of Donald Trump really kind of woke me up and slapped me because look, I've had to apologize. Some of what I did helped lead to Trump. some of the ugly personal politics that I got into help lead to Donald Trump. And Trump's election kind of woke me up and made me realize, oh my God, have I ever sounded like that? And on one of the issues like Black Lives Matter, look, if we were having this conversation five years ago and you would have said Black Lives Matter to me, right away, I would have said, no, all lives matter.",
