    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "We're kind of homeless now. There are a bunch of us. We don't belong in the Republican Party. There's no room for us. Liz Cheney is finding that out right now. We're not Democrats. Now, there's there are some of us who want to join the Democratic Party and try to move it more to the middle. But I think guys, I think we're at the precipice of real revolutionary change in America. I think sometime within the next few years, you're going to see a viable new third party because the Republican Party under Trump, it's shrinking. It still generally is the party of all white guys and all white gals and they're dying. Young people want nothing to do with the Republican Party. So I think there's an opportunity for a kind of a centrist third party.",
